> Would it be all right to apply the horn if you first wielded it?  Or
> is it a two-handed weapon?  (Been a while since I played.)

The unicorn horn is a two-handed weapon, but you don't have to wield it
to apply it. In fact <trying things out in explore mode, with a cursed
quarterstaff welded to my hands> you don't need any free hands at all
to apply it.

You'd have to unwield your weapon to loot a box or use a bag, though.

> What about wands?  Do you have to wield them (or at least unwield your
> weapon) before you can zap them?

No, you don't need any hands for that either.

> For that matter, I can think of a lot of actions that would probably
> require at least one empty hand.  I don't think I could eat a
> sandwich, drink from a bottle, or put on or take off clothing with the
> same hand I was holding a broadsword with, at least without risking a
> really nasty cut...

Not in NetHack. Obviously, you're either implicitly unwielding and
re-wielding your weapon, or it's a question of (pun intended)
handwaving.

